DEC-167 (the author, 2026-11-22): the sheaf clause of `defi:causalite` is read WITH gluing; every
ETT causality is absolutely minimal; precausality without gluing stays the underlying notion.

## What is defined

* `Precausality.CoverGluing`: the gluing axiom of a (co)sheaf with values in `𝐂`, as printed for a
  sheaf — for **every open `U` and every open cover of `U`**, `≤_U` and `≪_U` are the relations
  generated by those of the members (the colimit in `𝐂`).
* `Precausality.Glues`: the hereditary form `∀ W, AbsolutelyMinimalOn W`, and
  `Precausality.glues_iff_coverGluing`: **the two are the same condition**.
* `GluedCausality M`: a library `Causality` (the paper's "equivalently" form, no gluing) together
  with the field `glues`. The strict `Causality` is untouched (frozen during the wave); this
  structure is what `Causality` becomes under the refactor (plan in the REPORT).

## What is proved

* **Every glued causality is absolutely minimal**, on `M` and on every open set
  (`GluedCausality.absolutelyMinimal`, `.absolutelyMinimalOn`). Constructors: from causal
  arc-connectedness, from absolute minimality on `M` plus local causal arc-connectedness, time
  reversal, the restriction to an open subset as a spacetime of its own (`onOpen`), the pull-back
  along a local homeomorphism; the timelike and lightlike lines.
* `prop:GX_espace_temps_topo` **as printed, under gluing**: `existsUnique_gluedCausality_GX`
  (existence and uniqueness among glued causalities; over the maximal atlas, DEC-16; `G` acting by
  strong morphisms, DEC-12).
* `ex:open_subset`, **second sentence as printed, under gluing** (hereditary form; uniqueness
  also in the M-only form): `existsUnique_gluedCausality_localIsomorphism`. **First sentence: existence** (`GluedCausality.onOpen`,
  `onOpen_strongMorphism`) **but uniqueness is FALSE under gluing** (`not_openSubset_unique`; the
  diagonal causality glues and makes the inclusion strong), the cause being the direction of a
  strong morphism, not gluing (OQ-107). True forms, proved: the restriction is the greatest
  (`le_onOpen_of_strongMorphism`), the unique one whose inclusion reflects the relations
  (`eq_onOpen_of_reflects`), and the unique one making the inclusion a local isomorphism
  (`existsUnique_onOpen_localIsomorphism`).
* `rem:deux_pushup` under gluing: **"neither implies the other" is FALSE**. Push-up does not
  imply plainness (the lightlike line glues: `lightlike_pushUp_not_plain`), but on every `T1`
  space — so on every topological spacetime — **plainness implies push-up**
  (`GluedCausality.pushUp_of_causallyPlain`); the printed independence is refuted
  (`not_deux_pushup_neither`), and its no-gluing witness `deuxPushup` does not glue.
* `cexemple:point_transparent` under gluing: the transparent-point line is absolutely minimal on
  `ℝ` and **does not glue** (`transparentLine_not_glues`), so in the hereditary reading "This is a
  topological spacetime" (`ETT.tex:478`) is false; the sentence it illustrates, "Absolute
  minimality is not inherited by open subsets" (`ETT.tex:470`), is false for glued causalities
  (`GluedCausality.onOpen_absolutelyMinimal`) and true for precausalities (the strict
  `point_transparent`). In the M-only reading the line is a causality whose restriction to
  `ℝ ∖ {0}` is none (`transparentLine_onOpen_not_absolutelyMinimal`).

